  "text": "Welcome to Veterinary Medical Center of Long Island\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout\nOur Hospital\nOur Commitment\nVeterinary Specialists\nEmergency Veterinarians\nLeadership Team\nHospital Tour\nResidencies & Internships\nCareers\n24/7 Emergency & Critical Care\nSpecialty Services\nAcupuncture\nAnesthesia\nAvian & Exotic\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nHemodialysis\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology\nMedical Oncology\nRadiation Oncology\nOphthalmology\nPhysical Therapy\nSurgery\nDiagnostics\nRDVM Referrals\nClients\nClient Services Center\nNew Client Registration Form\nNew Client Specialist Forms\nRequest a Refill\nMake a Payment\nFinancing & Payment Plans\nAnimal Assistance Fund\nClient Feedback Form\nVeterinary Blog & News\nPet Loss & Grief Support\nContact\nContinuing Education\nCE Login\nSearch\nSearch\nFacebook\nGoogleBusiness\nSkip to Main Content\nAccessible Version\nStandard Version\n75 Sunrise Hwy North Service Rd\nWest Islip\nNY\n11795\nUS\n(631) 587-0800\nFacebook\nGoogleBusiness\nDonate\nContinuing Education\nCE Login\nAbout\nOur Hospital\nOur Commitment\nVeterinary Specialists\nEmergency Veterinarians\nLeadership Team\nHospital Tour\nResidencies & Internships\nCareers\n24/7 Emergency & Critical Care\nSpecialty Services\nAcupuncture\nAnesthesia\nAvian & Exotic\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nHemodialysis\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology\nMedical Oncology\nRadiation Oncology\nOphthalmology\nPhysical Therapy\nSurgery\nDiagnostics\nRDVM Referrals\nClients\nClient Services Center\nNew Client Registration Form\nNew Client Specialist Forms\nRequest a Refill\nMake a Payment\nFinancing & Payment Plans\nAnimal Assistance Fund\nClient Feedback Form\nVeterinary Blog & News\nPet Loss & Grief Support\nContact\nOpen Search Dialog\nHelp make emergency care available to clients and pets in need. Donate Now!\n×\nClose\nSearch\nSearch\nSpecialized Care You Can Count On\nSpecialty & Emergency Veterinary Care in Long Island, NY\nOur specialty veterinary services go beyond traditional veterinary medicine. We also offer emergency services 24 hours a day for times when your primary care veterinarian is unavailable.\nAbout Our Hospital\n24/7 Emergency Care\nAt VMCLI, our veterinarians offer emergency medicine and triage 24 hours, 7 days a week.\nLearn More\nSpecialty Services\nOur board-certified specialists provide advanced care in a variety of veterinary specialties.\nLearn More\nReferrals\nWe accept referrals from primary vets to provide specialty veterinary care services to companions.\nLearn More\nContinuing Education\nNew York state-approved continuing education for licensed veterinarians and technicians.\nLearn More\nWe're Here For You & Your Pets\nWelcome to the\nVeterinary Medical Center of Long Island\nVMCLI is a 28,000-square-foot, state-of-the-art, 24-hour emergency and multi-specialty veterinary hospital. Located in West Islip, we proudly serve cats, dogs and exotic pets on Long Island.\nWe know that the connection to your pet lasts a lifetime. Next to you and your family, your veterinarian is one of the most important people in your pet’s life.\nOur caring approach emphasizes an efficient and accurate diagnosis, with the use of the least invasive, yet effective, techniques to address your pet's medical issue.\nWe are committed to providing cutting-edge veterinary medicine and sharing this knowledge and expertise with both pet owners and referring family veterinarians.\nOur veterinarians specialize in critical emergency care but also offer a variety of other specialty services to meet the needs of pets with more complex health conditions.\nOur team of veterinary experts is proud to live up to more than 900 standards of veterinary excellence laid out by the American Animal Hospital Association.\nAbout Our Hospital\n24/7 Emergency Care\nAt VMCLI, our experienced veterinary team is prepared to diagnose and treat your companion animal in all types of emergency and critical care situations. Our team is trained to provide the quality care your pet needs 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.\nLearn More\nAdvanced Veterinary Care\nSpecialty Veterinary Services by Board-Certified Specialists\nOur hospital is staffed by a dedicated team of veterinary specialists with a shared commitment to providing world-class care to pets with complex needs.\nWorking closely with primary care veterinarians, our board-certified specialists provide next-level diagnosis and treatment for pets with the most challenging medical conditions. From\ncancer care\nand\nophthalmology\nto\nneurology\nand\ncardiology\n, your animal companion is in good hands.\nView Specialties\nVeterinary Medical Center of Long Island is by far the BEST place to bring your pets in an emergency situation. Everyone is knowledgeable and caring from the moment you arrive. Took me in immediately after explaining what my dog Stella was experiencing. Got back to me quickly with what her situation was. I then felt at ease and confident that they were doing the right thing.\n- Craig\nAccredited Online Courses\nCenter of Excellence for Veterinary Continuing Education\nVeterinary Medical Center of Long Island\nis a New York State-approved provider of continuing education for Licensed Veterinary Professionals.\nWhether you’re a licensed veterinarian or veterinary technician, VMCLI has continuing education offerings for you. You can receive high-quality CE at your own pace, with our free accredited online courses.\nLearn More\nHelping You Care For Your Pets\nPet Care Tips & Resources\nOur informative blogs feature helpful tips and advice from our Long Island veterinary specialists to help you to keep your pets healthy and happy.\nProud to Announce That We Are Still AAHA Accredited!\nPosted in\nHospital News\n,\nPet Care Tips\nThe VMCLI is proud to announce we have once again passed our American Animal Hospital Association (AAHA) accreditation recertification!\nRead more\nCat Eye Infections - Symptoms & Treatments\nPosted in\nPet Care Tips\nEye problems can be very painful for your cat and are often contagious. Today, we discuss a variety of eye issues seen in cats, signs, and how infections and other conditions are treated.\nRead more\nChronic Degenerative Valve Disease in Dogs\nPosted in\nPet Care Tips\nChronic degenerative valve disease is a form of heart disease often seen in small dogs. Here, we look at the causes, symptoms and treatment of this serious heart condition.\nRead more\nWhere to Find Our Clinic\nAddress & Hours\nVMCLI proudly offers emergency veterinary services 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. We also provide advanced veterinary specialty care and diagnostic services to patients on Long Island and beyond.\nHours of Operation\nMonday:\n24 hours\nTuesday:\n24 hours\nWednesday:\n24 hours\nThursday:\n24 hours\nFriday:\n24 hours\nSaturday:\n24 hours\nSunday:\n24 hours\nLocation\n75 Sunrise Hwy North Service Rd\nWest Islip\nNY\n11795\nUS\nPhone Number\n(631) 587-0800\nGet in Touch\nCaring for Pets on Long Island\nVeterinary Medical Center of Long Island\naccepts new clients to our specialty services by referral. Our 24/7 emergency service accepts all clients.\nContact Us\nLocation\n75 Sunrise Hwy North Service Rd\nWest Islip\nNY\n11795\nUS\nPhone Number\n(631) 587-0800\nContact\nSend us a message online.\nHours\nMonday:\n24 hours\nTuesday:\n24 hours\nWednesday:\n24 hours\nThursday:\n24 hours\nFriday:\n24 hours\nSaturday:\n24 hours\nSunday:\n24 hours\nAbout\n24/7 Emergency\nSpecialty Services\nRDVM Referrals\nContact\nVeterinary Medical Center of Long Island\nEmail Login\nDo Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\nDayforce Login\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms & Conditions\nAccessibility\nSearch\nSitemap\nBack to Top\nFacebook\nGoogleBusiness\nCopyright © 2026. All Rights Reserved.\nPart of the\nPetVet Care Centers Network\n.\nContact\nCall\n(631) 587-0800\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu",
